{
  "slug": "find-minimum-in-rotated-sorted-array",
  "title": "Find Minimum in Rotated Sorted Array",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": [
    "array",
    "binary-search"
  ],
  "license": "MIT",
  "source": {
    "name": "Mockify seed set"
  },
  "description": "A sorted array of **distinct** integers was rotated some number of times (e.g. `[0,1,2,4,5,6,7]` → `[4,5,6,7,0,1,2]`). Return the minimum element in O(log n).\n\n### Input\n- Line 1: `nums`, space-separated integers.\n\n### Output\nOne integer.\n\n### Constraints\n- `1 <= nums.length <= 6000`\n- `-5000 <= nums[i] <= 5000`\n- All values are distinct.",
  "signature": {
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "nums",
        "type": "int[]"
      }
    ],
    "returns": "int"
  },
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "3 4 5 1 2\n",
      "output": "1\n"
    },
    {
      "input": "4 5 6 7 0 1 2\n",
      "output": "0\n"
    },
    {
      "input": "11 13 15 17\n",
      "output": "11\n",
      "explanation": "Not rotated (or rotated a full cycle)."
    }
  ],
